$audio_instruct — audio + prompt → text (Qwen2-Audio 7B Instruct 4-bit)

SUMMARY
  Answers a text prompt about each sounds[] file using
  alicekyting/Qwen2-Audio-7B-Instruct-4bit (4-bit, GPU).

SYNTAX
  $audio_instruct
  $audio_instruct(prompt='What does the person say?')
  $audio_instruct(model='4bit', max_tokens=256)

INPUT
  sounds[]   — required; wav, mp3, flac, m4a, …
  prompts[]  — question or instruction per clip (or instruction body / prompt=)

OUTPUT
  texts[] — one model reply per audio file

ARGUMENTS
  prompt=     — same text for every clip (overrides prompts[])
  system=     — system message (default: You are a helpful assistant.)
  model=      — default | 4bit | qwen2-audio
  max_tokens= — generation cap (default 1024; use for long JSON)
  gpu=        — must be true / CUDA available (default: auto-detect)

MODELS
  models/qwen-audio/Qwen2-Audio-7B-Instruct-4bit/
  First run: uv run python tools/download_models.py --upstream-fallback

DEPENDENCIES
  uv sync --extra media   (torch, transformers, bitsandbytes, librosa)
  CUDA GPU required

ENVIRONMENT
  AH_EMULATE_AUDIO_INSTRUCT=1 — placeholder text, no model load.
  AH_AUDIO_INSTRUCT_GPU=1     — default gpu=True when arg omitted.

EXAMPLE
  @qa: $file('clip.wav') -> $audio_instruct
  What is being said?

  @describe: @track -> $audio_instruct(prompt='Describe the music briefly.')

PROMPT-CONSUMING
  Yes — prompts[] are used as the user question and cleared on output.
